DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     PPP is the protocol used for establishing internet links over dial-up
     modems, DSL connections, and many other types of point-to-point links.
     The ppppppdd daemon works together with the kernel ppp(4) driver to establish
     and maintain a PPP link with another system (called the _p_e_e_r) and to ne‐
     gotiate Internet Protocol (IP) addresses for each end of the link.  ppppppdd
     can also authenticate the peer and/or supply authentication information
     to the peer.  PPP can be used with other network protocols besides IP,
     but such use is becoming increasingly rare.

