NNOOTTEESS
     Some limited degree of control can be exercised over a running ppppppdd
     process by sending it a signal from the list below.

     SIGINT, SIGTERM
             These signals cause ppppppdd to terminate the link (by closing LCP),
             restore the serial device settings, and exit.

     SIGHUP  This signal causes ppppppdd to terminate the link, restore the serial
             device settings, and close the serial device.  If the ppeerrssiisstt or
             ddeemmaanndd option has been specified, ppppppdd will try to reopen the se‐
             rial device and start another connection (after the holdoff pe‐
             riod).  Otherwise ppppppdd will exit.  If this signal is received
             during the holdoff period, it causes ppppppdd to end the holdoff pe‐
             riod immediately.

     SIGUSR1
             This signal toggles the state of the ddeebbuugg option.

     SIGUSR2
             This signal causes ppppppdd to renegotiate compression.  This can be
             useful to re-enable compression after it has been disabled as a
             result of a fatal decompression error.  (Fatal decompression er‐
             rors generally indicate a bug in one or other implementation.)

